    {
      "id": "84181a70d4253e8930c4802e1be9431abc61b148",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 810117092,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Is the workaround ok for the time being?\n\nYes.  I've dredged up the work I'd done on doing this better, and can remove the workaround in TShark when that's done.\n\nNote that Wireshark, not TShark, is the exception here; Wireshark reads in the entire file before writing any files, so it has the complete file, but TShark, unless run with the `-2` option, writes as it reads, as do other programs such as editcap and mergecap.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
